# BARE-METAL MICROKERNEL SPECIFICATION & HARDWARE TOKEN FRAMEWORK

File: audit/baremetal_microkernel_spec.oot
Architecture blueprint for native openOODA bare-metal execution.

## 1. Overview & Objective

The openOODA Bare-Metal Microkernel framework extends the language's Zero-Trust Capability Model from user space directly onto bare hardware (x86_64, AArch64, RISC-V).

Instead of running atop a POSIX host OS kernel (Linux/macOS/Windows), the runtime directly interfaces with CPU privilege level 0 / EL1 / M-mode.
Zero Ambient Authority governs all hardware access:
No instruction may access memory-mapped I/O, reconfigure page tables, or enable interrupts without an explicit, unforgeable hardware capability token.

## 2. Hardware Capability Token Taxonomy

| Capability Token | Hardware Resource Managed | Kernel Privilege Gate |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `&HwCap` | Root hardware authority (mints child device tokens) | Bootloader / Core 0 Init |
| `&MmuCap` | Page table directory allocation & frame mapping | CR3 / TTBR0 / satp control |
| `&InterruptCap` | Interrupt Vector Table (IVT / IDT) & GIC / APIC | LIDT / CPU IRQ masking |
| `&UartCap` | Serial UART MMIO registers (TX/RX FIFO) | Peripheral MMIO address window |
| `&TimerCap` | Hardware system timer & preemption scheduler | PIT / Local APIC Timer / SysTick |
| `&DmaCap` | Direct Memory Access engine & IOMMU boundaries | PCIe bus master / IOMMU domain |

## 3. Microkernel Layered Architecture

```
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                  APPLICATIONS & ISOLATED DOMAINS (EL0)                  |
|  • Pure .oo applications holding attenuated capability tokens           |
|  • Zero ambient system authority                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                    │  Syscall IPC (Capability Transfer)
                                    ▼
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                 CAPABILITY ROUTER & IPC SUPERVISOR (EL1)                |
|  • Verifies HMAC capability seals on context switches                   |
|  • Enforces memory page isolation (NX bit, read-only .text)             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                    │
                                    ▼
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                    HARDWARE ABSTRACTION LAYER (HAL)                     |
|  • File: std/embedded_hal/mmu_token_map.oo                              |
|  • MMU Page Directory Management (mmu_map_frame)                        |
|  • Interrupt Vector Registration (interrupt_vector_entry_new)           |
|  • Serial MMIO Telemetry (uart_port_descriptor_new)                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                    │
                                    ▼
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                         PHYSICAL HARDWARE                               |
|  • x86_64 Long Mode / AArch64 EL1 / RISC-V S-mode Memory & Peripherals  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## 4. Execution Roadmap & Phase Alignment

1. **Phase 1 (Current - Framework Established)**:
   - Hardware capability structures defined in `std/embedded_hal/mmu_token_map.oo`.
   - MMU page entry bitmasks, interrupt vector descriptors, and MMIO ports modeled and verified via `fixtures/prove_prod_g4_emb_mmu_token_map.oo`.

2. **Phase 2 (Compiler Completion Gate)**:
   - Await completion of ongoing compiler lowerings (LLVM backend / direct ELF emitter) by compiler engineering squad.
   - Prevent premature fragmentation by keeping kernel implementation focused on HAL interfaces until standalone bare-metal codegen is certified.

3. **Phase 3 (Core Kernel Implementation)**:
   - Implement `core/microkernel/boot.oo` (multiboot2 / UEFI entry point).
   - Implement `core/microkernel/scheduler_round_robin.oo` with `&TimerCap` preemption.
   - Implement `core/microkernel/ipc_fast_channel.oo` for zero-copy capability passing.

4. **Phase 4 (Hardware Verification & QEMU Test Rail)**:
   - Target QEMU virt (`-M virt` for AArch64/RISC-V and `-M q35` for x86_64).
   - 5-stage Skeptic Prober test harness executing bare-metal binaries in automated headless QEMU.
